Chapter: RealBitcastF64

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 real-to-bits and bits-to-real, the f64 pair. Bare metal emits mov-rr for both --
 which is to say nothing at all: it holds a Real f64 as its own bits in a general
 register, so the value and its pattern are the same sixty-four bits. Zig
 separates the two types, so the identity is spelled @bitCast there. Every answer
 below is an Integer, which `show` reads exactly, so no line depends on how a Real
 prints.

 THE FIRST BLOCK IS GROUND TRUTH, patterns anyone can check against IEEE-754 by
 hand: 1.0 is #3FF0000000000000, 0.5 is #3FE0000000000000, 42.5 is
 #4045400000000000. They pin the exponent bias and the mantissa placement, which
 an emitter reaching for a CONVERSION instead of a cast gets wrong immediately --
 real-to-int of 1.0 is 1, not 4607182418800017408.

 THE SECOND BLOCK IS WHAT A CONVERSION CANNOT DO, and it is the reason this pair
 is worth a test of its own rather than a line in the conversion one.

   NEGATIVE ZERO is a value Real comparison cannot see: -0.0 == 0.0 is true, so
   nothing else in the language distinguishes them. Its bits are INT64_MIN and
   +0.0's are 0. A truncating emitter answers 0 for both and passes every test
   that does not look here.

   A NaN has no equal, itself included, so its PATTERN is the only evidence it
   survived a round trip. #7FF8000000000000 must come back unchanged; an emitter
   that routes through an arithmetic register on a platform that quiets signalling
   NaNs would not.

   INFINITY and the largest finite double sit one bit apart -- #7FF0000000000000
   and #7FEFFFFFFFFFFFFF -- and a conversion answers "integer indefinite" for the
   first while the second is far past what an i64 holds. Bits distinguish them.

 TOTALITY IS THE LAST LINE. Every i64 names an f64 and every f64 has a pattern,
 so unlike real-to-int there is no range to fall out of and nothing to guard. The
 round trip through the bit pattern of the largest finite double is the widest
 that claim gets tested.

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("bits 0.0 " & show (real-to-bits 0.0))
    print-line-uni ("bits 1.0 " & show (real-to-bits 1.0))
    print-line-uni ("bits 0.5 " & show (real-to-bits 0.5))
    print-line-uni ("bits 42.5 " & show (real-to-bits 42.5))
    print-line-uni ("bits -1.0 " & show (real-to-bits (0.0 - 1.0)))
    print-line-uni ("bits -2.0 " & show (real-to-bits (0.0 - 2.0)))
    print-line-uni ("negzero " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #8000000000000000)))
    print-line-uni ("poszero " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #0)))
    print-line-uni ("nan " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #7FF8000000000000)))
    print-line-uni ("inf " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #7FF0000000000000)))
    print-line-uni ("maxfinite " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real #7FEFFFFFFFFFFFFF)))
    print-line-uni ("roundtrip 42.5 " & show (real-to-bits (bits-to-real (real-to-bits 42.5))))
  end
